meta {
  name: Internal - Whalesync
  seq: 20
}

headers {
  X-Scratch-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}
}

docs {
  Internal, admin-only server-to-server channel (`/internal/whalesync/*`) that
  Bottlenose/Whalesync uses to provision shadow users and mint session tokens.

  These endpoints use a DIFFERENT auth pattern than the rest of the collection:
  the shared-secret header `X-Scratch-Admin-Token` (added here at the folder level),
  compared against the server's `SCRATCH_ADMIN_API_KEY`. Set the secret `adminToken`
  environment variable to that key. There is no user session — each endpoint acts on
  the shadow user named in the request body/path: by `whalesyncTeamId` for a Whalesync
  team's (the "Team" requests), or by `whalesyncUserId` for one made for a person before
  teams.

  (The collection's inherited `Authorization: API-Token` header is ignored by these
  routes, so it is harmless that it is still sent.)
}
